    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## \ud83e\uddfe Invoice Intake and Logging\npowered by easybits\n\n**What it does**\nWatches a Gmail inbox for unread emails with attachments, extracts the fields from any invoice it finds, logs new invoices to a Google Sheet, and sends a Telegram alert. Duplicate invoices are skipped automatically.\n\n**How it works**\n1. The Gmail trigger polls every minute for unread mail and downloads attachments.\n2. The Code node keeps only real attachments (drops inline images under 10 KB) and normalizes each one to the `data` binary key.\n3. Loop Over Items processes one attachment per run, which the Extractor requires.\n4. Supported file types (PDF, JPEG, PNG, WebP) go to the easybits Extractor, which returns the invoice fields plus a `document_class`.\n5. Only documents classed as `invoice` continue. The sheet is checked by invoice number, and only unseen invoices are appended and announced on Telegram.\n\n**Set up steps**\n1. Gmail trigger: connect your Gmail OAuth2 credential. Attachment download is already enabled.\n2. Extractor: add your easybits Extractor credential and build a pipeline returning `document_class`, `invoice_number`, `vendor_name`, `service_name`, `service_period`, `total_net`, `vat_amount`, `total_gross`.\n3. Google Sheets (both nodes): select your invoice spreadsheet and tab. Column headers must match the field names above.\n4. Telegram: set your bot credential and replace the chat ID with your own.\n5. Activate the workflow.",
        "height": 688,
        "width": 512
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -592,
        -208
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "20fbe76c-3b28-4e0b-bf53-98b30c458a0c",
      "name": "Sticky Note4"
    }
